<article class="env-example" id="04V1">
<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/04V1">Example <span data-tag="04V1">4.7.4.17</span>.</a> Let $X$ be a Kan complex, which we regard as an object of the $\infty $-category of spaces $\operatorname{\mathcal{S}}$ (Construction <a data-tag="00TZ" href="/tag/00TZ">3.1.6.1</a>). Then: </p>
<p><ul>
<li><p>
The Kan complex $X$ is a discrete object of the $\infty $-category $\operatorname{\mathcal{S}}$ (in the sense of Definition <a data-tag="05EY" href="/tag/05EY">4.7.4.13</a>) if and only if every connected component of $X$ is contractible: that is, the projection map $X \rightarrow \pi _0(X)$ is a homotopy equivalence. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
The Kan complex $X$ is a subterminal object of the $\infty $-category $\operatorname{\mathcal{S}}$ (in the sense of Definition <a data-tag="04UY" href="/tag/04UY">4.7.4.1</a>) if and only if $X$ is either empty or contractible. 
</p>
</li>
</ul></p>
<p> See Example <a data-tag="05EF" href="/tag/05EF">4.7.1.8</a>. </p>
</article>
